{{- /*
  The collection surface: one card per source kind, each carrying the pair that
  governs its polling, the record rate opnview has measured, and the pair it would
  suggest.

  THE ROUTE NAMES ITSELF ONCE, AND EACH CARD NAMES ITS KIND. There is one <h1> for
  the route and one <h2> per card beneath it, and every card is labelled by that
  heading through aria-labelledby, so arriving cold the page says what it is and
  that the cards are instances of one thing rather than four unrelated panels. The
  group headings inside a card are <h3>, under the card's own name.

  ONE CARD PER KIND AND ONE SAVE PER CARD, angular at the 0.25rem radius — the
  layout docs/ui-references.md's General layout row records, and the same card the
  settings surface already uses. Each card is its own form, because a value refused
  on one kind must leave the other three saveable; a single form over four kinds
  could not manage that. The cards are the kinds the `provider` table actually
  holds, read at runtime: a kind with no implementation on this installation
  produces no card at all.

  THE THREE GROUPS ARE THREE GROUPS DELIBERATELY. The page size in force and the
  page size suggested are two separately labelled figures under two separate
  headings, because a reader who confused them would read a proposal as a setting.

  WHAT A CARD HAS TO SAY, IT SAYS INSIDE ITSELF. A save confirmed, a suggestion put
  into the fields, a figure refused: each is drawn in the card it belongs to, and a
  refusal is drawn against the FIELD that caused it — marked aria-invalid, pointed
  at the refusal by aria-describedby, and given the focus. A banner at the top of a
  page four cards tall names neither the kind that was saved nor the field that was
  refused.

  A FIGURE IS DATA AND A STATE IS A STRING. Every label, every heading and every
  state below is a catalogue lookup; the only text that is not is a measured figure
  — a count, a rate, a number of seconds, an instant. Where there is no figure to
  show, a NAMED STATE is shown instead and never a nought: no record in the window,
  no second clock on this table, a span too short to divide by and a source nobody
  is reading are four different conditions and they render as four different
  sentences.

  THE FILL CONTROL WRITES NOTHING, AND IS NOT OFFERED WITH NOTHING TO FILL. It puts
  the suggested figures into the fields, exactly as the settings surface's fetch
  control fills the fingerprint field, and the save beside it is the second
  deliberate act; where the card's outcome state carries no pair the control is
  disabled, because a control that is offered changes what the product does.

  EACH IMPLEMENTATION HAS ITS OWN SELECTION, in its kind's card and saved with it:
  left to the probe round, collected whatever the probe found, or declined. The
  three choices are named by the states they put the implementation in, the same
  sentences the in-force group reports, so the choice and its effect read alike.

  THE FIELDS STAY TYPEABLE IN EVERY STATE, including a kind whose source is
  unavailable: an operator sizing for a source they are about to switch on is the
  ordinary case. A kind whose page opnview cannot set says so WHERE THE SECOND FIELD
  WOULD BE, which is the only place that answers why the form offers one.

  NOTHING HERE WRITES TO THE FIREWALL, and nothing on this page makes any outbound
  call at all: every figure is read from the local database.
*/ -}}
{{define "body" -}}
<h1>{{t "collection.title"}}</h1>
{{- range .CollectionCards}}
<section class="card" id="card_{{.Kind}}" aria-labelledby="card_name_{{.Kind}}">
<h2 id="card_name_{{.Kind}}">{{t .LabelKey}}</h2>
{{- with .NoticeKey}}
<p class="notice ok">{{t .}}</p>
{{- end}}
<form method="post" action="{{$.CollectionPath}}">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{$.CSRFToken}}">
<input type="hidden" name="{{.FieldKind}}" value="{{.Kind}}">

<h3>{{t "collection.group.in_force"}}</h3>
<dl class="states">
{{- range .InForce}}
<dt>{{t .LabelKey}}</dt>
<dd>{{if .StateKey}}{{t .StateKey}}{{else}}<span class="figure">{{.Value}}</span>{{end}}</dd>
{{- end}}
</dl>

<h3>{{t "collection.group.measurement"}}</h3>
<dl class="states">
{{- range .Measurement}}
<dt>{{t .LabelKey}}</dt>
<dd>{{if .StateKey}}{{t .StateKey}}{{else}}<span class="figure">{{.Value}}</span>{{end}}</dd>
{{- end}}
</dl>
{{- if .Gaps}}
<table class="gaps">
<thead>
<tr><th>{{t "collection.label.gap_reason"}}</th><th>{{t "collection.label.gap_count"}}</th><th>{{t "collection.label.missed_seconds"}}</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Gaps}}
<tr><td>{{t .ReasonKey}}</td><td><span class="figure">{{.Count}}</span></td><td><span class="figure">{{.MissedSeconds}}</span></td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
{{- end}}

<h3>{{t "collection.group.suggestion"}}</h3>
<dl class="states">
{{- range .Suggestion}}
<dt>{{t .LabelKey}}</dt>
<dd>{{if .StateKey}}{{t .StateKey}}{{else}}<span class="figure">{{.Value}}</span>{{end}}</dd>
{{- end}}
</dl>

<h3>{{t "collection.group.implementations"}}</h3>
{{- $card := .}}
{{- range .Implementations}}
{{- if eq $card.InvalidField .Field}}
<div class="field invalid">
<label for="{{.Field}}_{{$card.Kind}}">{{t .LabelKey}}</label>
<select id="{{.Field}}_{{$card.Kind}}" name="{{.Field}}" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{.Field}}_refusal_{{$card.Kind}}" autofocus>
{{- range .Options}}
<option value="{{.Value}}"{{if .Selected}} selected{{end}}>{{t .LabelKey}}</option>
{{- end}}
</select>
<p class="field-refusal" id="{{.Field}}_refusal_{{$card.Kind}}">{{t $card.RefusalKey}}</p>
</div>
{{- else}}
<div class="field">
<label for="{{.Field}}_{{$card.Kind}}">{{t .LabelKey}}</label>
<select id="{{.Field}}_{{$card.Kind}}" name="{{.Field}}">
{{- range .Options}}
<option value="{{.Value}}"{{if .Selected}} selected{{end}}>{{t .LabelKey}}</option>
{{- end}}
</select>
</div>
{{- end}}
{{- end}}

{{- if .PageIsAdjustable}}
{{- if eq .InvalidField .FieldPageSize}}
<div class="field invalid">
<label for="page_size_{{.Kind}}">{{t "field.page_size"}}</label>
<input id="page_size_{{.Kind}}" name="{{.FieldPageSize}}" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" value="{{.PageSizeField}}" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="page_size_refusal_{{.Kind}}" autofocus>
<p class="field-refusal" id="page_size_refusal_{{.Kind}}">{{t .RefusalKey}}</p>
</div>
{{- else}}
<div class="field">
<label for="page_size_{{.Kind}}">{{t "field.page_size"}}</label>
<input id="page_size_{{.Kind}}" name="{{.FieldPageSize}}" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" value="{{.PageSizeField}}">
</div>
{{- end}}
{{- else}}
<div class="field">
<span class="label">{{t "field.page_size"}}</span>
<span class="field-state">{{t "state.sizing.page_not_adjustable"}}</span>
</div>
{{- end}}
{{- if eq .InvalidField .FieldInterval}}
<div class="field invalid">
<label for="interval_{{.Kind}}">{{t "field.interval_seconds"}}</label>
<input id="interval_{{.Kind}}" name="{{.FieldInterval}}" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" value="{{.IntervalField}}" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="interval_refusal_{{.Kind}}" autofocus>
<p class="field-refusal" id="interval_refusal_{{.Kind}}">{{t .RefusalKey}}</p>
</div>
{{- else}}
<div class="field">
<label for="interval_{{.Kind}}">{{t "field.interval_seconds"}}</label>
<input id="interval_{{.Kind}}" name="{{.FieldInterval}}" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" value="{{.IntervalField}}">
</div>
{{- end}}
<div class="actions">
<button type="submit" name="{{.FieldFill}}" value="1" class="secondary"{{if not .SuggestionExists}} disabled{{end}}>{{t "action.fill_suggestion"}}</button>
<button type="submit">{{t "action.save"}}</button>
</div>
</form>
</section>
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
